  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186176053,
      "id": "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326",
      "title": "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "590618ea-351f-57a2-b27a-a7f31e5b3ea2",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\csc x$?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range is all real numbers.\n- **II.** The graph has a zero at $x=0$.\n- **III.** The function has no global minimum or maximum.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "159fef16-d6c9-5e3d-8cc7-014ae7fdd525",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "2668455a-7af0-5169-b108-0e3c2c690470",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "2779fa88-7c2e-5216-bd93-0f199258541e",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "2668455a-7af0-5169-b108-0e3c2c690470"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "e9c6624c-f1bf-5043-8030-fa8dacce4215",
          ":answer-field/key": "II",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "36689554-c905-5669-a429-168fd3c9a3bb",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "5fcea207-678a-5ba6-b0bc-f2e263b6993d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "36689554-c905-5669-a429-168fd3c9a3bb"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "069eefe9-e54c-5f01-a72f-0f74bb467ecd",
          ":answer-field/key": "III",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "2d6417a7-d4d1-5ed7-a694-5e0016bb9042",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "bcf363d8-0969-5cef-8082-0b880c0ec391",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "bcf363d8-0969-5cef-8082-0b880c0ec391"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\csc x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty,-1]\\cup[1,\\infty)$.  Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The cosecant graph does not intersect the $x$-axis. Hence, statement II is false.\n\n- The range is unbounded above and below, so the function has no global minimum or maximum. Hence, statement III is true.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy"
    },
